<li><strong>Hytrol</strong>, Jonesboro, AR. Full range of gravity, BDLR, CDLR, and MDR roller conveyors. One of the largest North American conveyor manufacturers with a nationwide integrator network.</li>
<li><strong>Interroll</strong>, Global. Manufactures MDR rollers (RollerDrive series), gravity roller modules, and conveyor platforms. Major OEM supplier to system integrators.</li>
<li><strong>Dematic</strong>, Global. System integrator offering MDR, BDLR, and CDLR roller conveyor systems for distribution and fulfillment.</li>
<li><strong>Intelligrated (Honeywell)</strong>, Mason, OH. Full conveyor system integrator with IntelliSort sortation and roller conveyor lines.</li>
<li><strong>TGW</strong>, Global. Integrated roller conveyor systems for e-commerce and distribution.</li>
<li><strong>Bastian Solutions (Toyota)</strong>, Indianapolis, IN. Conveyor system integrator specializing in distribution and fulfillment.</li>
<li><strong>Dorner</strong>, Hartland, WI. Precision roller and belt conveyors for packaging, assembly, and food processing.</li>
<li><strong>mk North America</strong>, Bloomfield, CT. Modular aluminum-frame roller and belt conveyors for packaging and automation.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What are the different types of roller conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The five main roller conveyor types are: <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/gravity/">gravity roller</a> (unpowered), belt-driven live roller or BDLR (single motor drives all rollers via belt), line-shaft roller (motor drives rollers via splined shaft and O-rings), <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR</a> (24VDC motors inside individual rollers), and <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a> (chain loops drive rollers via sprockets for heavy loads).</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">How do I choose between gravity and powered roller conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Choose <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/gravity/">gravity roller</a> when you have a slight decline (3-5 degrees), consistent product weights, and no need for speed control or <a href="/conveyor-types/accumulation-conveyors/">accumulation</a>. Choose <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/powered/">powered roller</a> when you need consistent speed, uphill transport, accumulation, or integration with <a href="/resources/automated-conveyor-systems/">automated systems</a>.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What roller spacing do I need?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>At least 3 rollers must contact the product bottom at all times. Divide your smallest product length by 3, then round down to the nearest standard pitch (1.5", 2", 3", 4.5", or 6"). A 12-inch long case needs 4-inch or smaller roller spacing. A 24-inch pallet needs 8-inch or smaller spacing.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What is the weight capacity of a roller conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Weight capacity depends on roller type. Standard gravity rollers: 75-200 lbs per product. BDLR: up to 500 lbs. <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR</a>: 150-250 lbs per zone. <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a>: 500-10,000+ lbs for <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">pallet applications</a>. Capacity depends on roller diameter, wall thickness, bearing type, and frame gauge.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">Why is MDR replacing line-shaft conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-5" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p><a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR technology</a> provides zero-pressure accumulation without pneumatics, uses 50%+ less energy (zones only run when needed), runs quieter (65 dB vs 80+ dB), requires less maintenance (no belts, chains, or O-rings), and supports easy zone-by-zone expansion. Interroll, Itoh Denki, and Rulmeca are leading MDR roller manufacturers.</p>

</div>
</div>
